{"context":"eka-steward is a new product that must drive a project through EKA without becoming a second source of truth. It needs read/write access to EKA knowledge and the ability to orchestrate external agent CLIs. The integration options with EKA are library import, CLI subprocess, or MCP.","decision":"eka-steward imports eka-core as a Go library pinned to v2 for all EKA operations; the eka CLI subprocess is an escape hatch for not-yet-librarized operations; MCP is rejected (extra hop, weaker determinism, larger trust surface). Steward is the SOLE EKA store writer; workers never write EKA. Steward is a separate repo, version 2.0.0, part of the EKA v2 program with its own tag/release train.","consequences":"One writer keeps the store coherent and auditable. Library pinning couples steward to eka-core v2 (intended). The escape hatch isolates any subprocess coupling behind one adapter. Rejecting MCP avoids a network/trust hop. Cost: steward must track eka-core v2 upgrades.","alternativesConsidered":"MCP-only integration (rejected: hop, non-determinism, trust surface). CLI-only integration (rejected: heavy per-call process, weaker typing). Embed eka-core into eka-cli and call it (rejected: couples release trains).","appliesTo":["eka-steward/**"]}